entityDescription:
The Syndicat Intercommunal d'Amenagement du Chablais (SIAC) is the public administrative body of the 62 municipalities of the Chablais. The SIAC is funded and governed by the municipalities via three groups of municipalities, (sub regions of the Chablais territory), known as Thonon Agglom&eacute;ration, Communaut&eacute; de communes de Haute Chablais (CCHC) and Communaut&eacute; de communes du Pays d&rsquo;Evian et de la Vall&eacute;e d&rsquo;Abondance (CCPEVA). This is a stable structure that was established in 2003.

The SIAC has 4 core missions across the Chablais:
- Chablais UNESCO Global Geopark;
- Territorial urban planning framework (SCoT);
- National and European Grant Administration;
- River Basin Management Contract.

The SIAC general committee comprises 55 elected politicians and an executive committee of 9 elected politicians. The SIAC president is Geraldine Pflieger (Mayor of Saint-Gingolph and a UNESCO chair in Water Politics, University of Geneva), Marie-Pierre Berthier (Mayor of Nernier) is the SIAC vice-president is responsible for the Chablais UGGp and is one of the official EGN representatives. The general and executive committees, as representatives of the local territory, make decisions concerning the Chablais region.
